# Legacy URL Redirects

Permanent **301** redirects are defined in [`apps/frontend/redirects.ts`](apps/frontend/redirects.ts) and wired in `next.config.ts` via `redirects()`.

| Legacy path | Destination |
|-------------|-------------|
| `/shop` | `/plp` |
| `/shop/:slug` | `/plp/category/:slug` |
| `/product/:slug` | `/pdp/:slug` |
| `/my-account` | `/account` |
| `/سوالات-متداول` | `/faq` |

## Notes

- Query strings are preserved automatically by Next.js.
- Trailing slashes are normalized in [`middleware.ts`](apps/frontend/middleware.ts) (`/shop/foo/` → `/shop/foo` → redirect to `/plp/category/foo`).
- Add new legacy paths to `legacyRedirects` in `redirects.ts`; keep the list in this rule in sync.

## Related

- FAQ page: `apps/frontend/src/app/(product)/faq/page.tsx` (`/faq`)
- PLP category: `apps/frontend/src/app/(product)/plp/category/[slug]/page.tsx`
- PDP: `apps/frontend/src/app/(product)/pdp/[slug]/page.tsx`
